 Production `train` now handles `Ctrl-C` and low-disk stops as durable interruptions: active MACE process groups are terminated gracefully, checkpoint bytes remain, interrupted attempts do not consume retry allowance, and the next invocation resumes with `--restart_latest`. Run-local records and valid final model/checkpoint artifacts recover parent-process commit gaps. Completed runs are SHA-256 re-inventoried and skipped; changed/missing checkpoint bytes fail closed rather than triggering silent recalculation. See `PATCH_NOTES_0.20.74a0.md`.
 
